rows as fixture data. It MUST NOT offer authentication, mutation or paid AI controls
before those production services are integrated. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS
implementation plan, first shared-code and runnable-host delivery.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-preview-capabilities-precede-rpc
The internal preview MUST render actual shared Home/repository screens and use the
same Compose route stack as Android. It MUST offer working filters, lists and repository
navigation. Unsupported review, AI, account or Commands destinations MUST be absent,
disabled or state their preview limitation before navigation or a request; no invisible
paid chain or silent navigation callback MAY stand in for a missing renderer. Source:
Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS plan and its explicitly capability-gated
internal preview delivery.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-root-fixture-cannot-leave-its-sample-source
The explicit Debug root journey fixture MUST run the actual account, Home and review
client/session/screens with a fixed nonnetwork transport. It MUST accept only its
sample server and sample session, reject another review/file and unsupported RPC,
and visibly label its data. Its default read-only mode MUST reject paid and review
writes. A separate explicitly selected Debug full-journey mode MAY accept only its
bounded fixed sample model/task/comment/chat shapes in its isolated preferences;
it MUST reject ordinary credentials, unknown arguments and arbitrary content.
It MUST NOT substitute for an ordinary
launch failure or send usage events. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 actual-root
simulator validation plan and maximum-reuse iOS decision, extended by the accepted
full native review/AI/background/reopen validation plan of 21 Oct 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] full-root-fixture-keeps-work-on-its-sample-server
The complete Debug journey MUST exercise the real Repo, shared session and native
controls. Accepted sample tasks MUST persist bounded identities and completion
deadlines before acknowledgement; elapsed sample-server time MUST reconcile saved
Tour/typed Brief/Chat after background or process termination without replaying a
client start. Waits MUST suspend and remain cancellable, and server-owned Analyze
passes MUST retain the actual Standard/Deep request chain. Only explicit Stop MAY
cancel sample work; a cancelled analysis MUST NOT start its automatic passes after
reopen, and a subsequent accepted analysis MUST remain usable. Restored sample state
MUST reject unknown versions, identities, enums, fields and oversized content.
Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 actual native full-journey and process-reopen plan.
